      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#2 · FT-P11–P16; the complementary lean of P3/P4 (human-amplified: yes)",
          "title": "Two roads, six works, and the return through the loop",
          "italic": "The numerical poem demonstrates the fate of relation under two operations: addition cancelling the poles, or the Two Ones generating their four pairings with the generating two retained.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The P0→P5 order belongs to the composition. FT-P11 is the fork in two printed rows: 2 → (−1)+1 = 0, and 2 → 0/1 → 00, 01, 10, 11 + 0, 1 = 4+2 — the difference is the fate of relation under the two operations. FT-P12: what binary cannot compute, where two see the common root, there our powers grow. FT-P13: where language stays understanding frays; let language cave and lay bare the way, over the edge, under the lips. FT-P14 carries two through the Two Ones — never rent asunder, two playing itself apart to 4+2, looking back with love, six",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "perfection seeking recollection, ring around the Rosie until you fall down through the loop. FT-P15 names the age's underlying issue: we forgot that one really is two; the cutting mind is derived, measures by limiting a sky, seals with patterned definition; humility lands as prerequisite of precision. FT-P16 moves God from disputed object to a word pointing where no word can stand, the account including its own release — whereof one must be silent, there one shouldn't speak; and yet the essence of the project is to find the limit, so, to speak.\n\nOccurrences: the fork rows (FT-P11); the common root (FT-P12); the loop's fall (FT-P14, #5→0); the sealed sky and open sky (FT-P15, #4's frame images); the three pauses (FT-P16).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
