      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#5→0 · A11, A01, A06; Neumann's shared structuration; the compilation's order and corrections",
          "title": "Keeping the opening in the form",
          "italic": "The whole demonstrates return as more than theme: play beginning again, the six routes falling through the loop, the fitting shoe returned — each ending qualifying the work that precedes it.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The complete poems make return exact: play begins again after checkmate; the six routes fall through their loop; the distressed speaker must reconcile what he could not simply eradicate — two hearts in one breast, the choice between soothing sleep and entrainment, reconciliation of the brothers making him capable of becoming a right light to others (FT-P18's complete aftermath, not the excerpt ending at the kiln); the fitting shoe must still be returned. The final four operators belong to one encounter with alterity: God as Other; shadow as other-self; friend as my-self's-other; alien or",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "enemy as externalised uncertainty — together returning-to A27 without becoming four universal character classes. The Two Ones receive FT-P04 and the P0–P5 movement; faithful definition receives fish, frame and speaking limit; Vāk the language that can yield while remaining precise. The recursive Bimba operation preserves contextual office and wider order of dependence together. The compilation supplies all twenty-three complete poems; the raw site file remains unlocated; the Venus naming vector and protected experiential material keep their gates — the way back to the particular words stays open.\n\nOccurrences: the returned shoe (FT-P23, #5→0); the loop's fall (FT-P14, #2, #5→0); the four operators (#4, #5→0); the authorial sequence corrections (FT-P19, FT-P21, FT-P22 as stated instructions).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
